      en: ["Ežerėlis was formally established as a settlement for peat miners in 1918.", "The town's name is derived from the Lithuanian word for 'small lake'.", "Ežerėlis was officially granted city status in the year 1956.", "The town's economy is historically tied to the 4,000-hectare Ežerėlis peat bog.", "A modern Roman Catholic church was built and consecrated in the town in 1998.", "The town is located approximately 25 kilometers west of Lithuania's second-largest city, Kaunas."],
